{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And she called to the men of the house, etc.</b> Because she knew the righteousness of Joseph in his master's eyes, and that he would not believe her words, therefore she planned it and called to them so that they would speak when her master came home — and this is the meaning of <b>to say</b>. She kindled in them the fire of jealousy to testify, and this is the meaning of <b>See, he brought us</b>, etc., <b>to mock us</b> — she drew them into her distress, for he was also raised over them and he is a foreign man." "<b>Or</b> it may intend in his saying <b>see</b>, that they would testify to the facts, for thus they saw — and this is the meaning of ״to say, see״. She also devised to complain against her husband, for by this means, if he speaks favorably on Joseph's behalf, she will say: ״Even this is among the reproofs against you, my complaint.״"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:06.914832731Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}